                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 1.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Field, Acting Attorney-General, to Mr. Pierrepont,
                        district attorney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Attorney-General’s
                            Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>,
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-08-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >August</hi> 3, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards Pierrepont</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">United States Attorney, New York City:</hi></p>
                <p><seg type="margin">[757]</seg> The Secretary of State informs this office that
                    the Peruvian minister has notified him that a state of war still exists between
                    Peru and Spain; that the Spanish government has ordered the building within the
                    United States of thirty gun-boats equipped for war, fifteen of *which are
                    building in the ship-yards of the Mystic River, Connecticut, ten in Poillon’s
                    yards, Brooklyn, New York, four of which last have been launched, and are at
                    Delamater’s, receiving engines; and five gun-boats are building at Green Point;
                    and that the President desires that you act promptly and prevent the sailing of
                    any of these gun-boats.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. A. FIELD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Attorney-General.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
